.\" Manual page for feel v2.2.0
.TH FEEL 1 "2026-08-13" "feel v2.2.0" "User Commands"
.
.SH NAME
feel \- record your current feelings from the command line
.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B feel
.RI [ subcommand ]
.RI [ arguments... ]
.
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B feel
is a simple command-line tool to record your moods or thoughts.
It supports interactive mode, direct recording, long-form notes,
listing, reading, and deletion of entries.
The language of its prompts and messages follows the
.B LANG
environment variable: Chinese when it starts with
.BR zh ,
English otherwise.
.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B feel
Start interactive recording mode. You are prompted for your feeling
and an optional note. Press Enter with no input at the feeling
prompt to exit.
.TP
.BI "feel " description
Record an entry directly with the given
.IR description .
.TP
.B feel long
Compose a long-form entry in an editor
.RB ( $EDITOR ,
default
.BR vim ).
A file is created in the long-form directory (see
.B FILES
below) with a default
.B #
heading of the form
.IR "unix_timestamp yyyy-mm-dd hh:mm" ,
and an index line is appended to the main log.
If no content is written, the entry is cancelled.
.TP
.BI "feel read " "timestamp | index | last"
Print the full content of a long-form entry, matched by its Unix
timestamp, by the line number shown by
.BR "feel list" ,
or by the keyword
.BR last
for the most recent entry.
.TP
.BR "feel show " "timestamp | index | last"
Alias for
.BR read .
.TP
.BR "feel list " [ \-n \fIN\fP ] [ \-a ]
Show log entries. By default the last 10 entries are shown.
Long-form entries are marked with a
.B [LONG]:
prefix and displayed with their
.B #
title (or
.I <no summary>
if the title was not customized).
.TP
.BI "feel delete " "timestamp | index | last"
Delete the entry matching the specified Unix timestamp, the line
number shown by
.BR "feel list" ,
or, with the keyword
.BR last ,
the most recent entry.
Deletion requires confirmation.
.TP
.B feel version
Print version information.
.TP
.BR "feel help " | \-h | \-\-help
Show a brief help message.
.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-n \fIN\fP
With
.BR list :
display the last
.I N
entries (e.g.,
.BR \-n " 5" ).
.TP
.B \-a
With
.BR list :
display all recorded entries.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Equivalent to
.BR help .
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Equivalent to
.BR version .
.
.SH ALIASES
For convenience,
.B feel
provides the following aliases:
.TP
.B ls
Equivalent to
.BR list .
.TP
.B "ls -a"
Equivalent to
.BR "list \-a" .
.TP
.BI "ls \-n " N
Equivalent to
.BI "list \-n " N .
.TP
.B show
Equivalent to
.BR read .
.TP
.BR del ", " rm
Equivalent to
.BR delete .
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Equivalent to
.BR help .
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Equivalent to
.BR version .
.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B LANG
Selects the display language. Values starting with
.B zh
produce Chinese messages; anything else produces English.
.TP
.B EDITOR
Editor used by
.BR "feel long" .
Defaults to
.BR vim .
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME
Base directory for data. Defaults to
.IR ~/.local/share .
.TP
.B FEEL_MD_EXT
When set to
.B true
(case-insensitive), the main log uses
.B log.txt
and long-form entries use the
.B .md
extension; otherwise the
.B .feel
extension is used (the default). The switch only affects newly
written files and leaves existing data untouched.
.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/feel/log.feel
Main log. Each line has the form
.IR "unix_timestamp yyyy-mm-dd hh:mm feeling [(note)]" .
With
.B FEEL_MD_EXT=true
this becomes
.IR log.txt .
.TP
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/feel/long/
Directory for long-form entries, one
.B .feel
file per entry (or
.B .md
with
.BR FEEL_MD_EXT=true ).
.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
An error occurred.
.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Start interactive recording:
.RS
.nf
$ feel
Feeling: The sun is shining
Note (optional, Enter to skip):
.fi
.RE
.PP
Record directly from the command line:
.RS
.nf
$ feel "Finished writing the manual page"
Recorded: 1786555500 2026-08-13 01:25 Finished writing the manual page
.fi
.RE
.PP
Compose a long-form entry in the editor:
.RS
.nf
$ feel long
.fi
.RE
.PP
Read the most recent long-form entry:
.RS
.nf
$ feel read last
.fi
.RE
.PP
View the last 5 entries:
.RS
.nf
$ feel list \-n 5
.fi
.RE
.PP
Show all entries with the alias:
.RS
.nf
$ feel ls \-a
.fi
.RE
.PP
Delete the most recent entry:
.RS
.nf
$ feel delete last
.fi
.RE
.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR date (1),
.BR vim (1),
.BR env (1)
.
